# The commands that had no button before there was a palette: selection, the other pane, view
# modes, sorting. Each is run by id, the way choosing it in the palette runs it.
#
# `run` goes through the same registry a key press does, so a command that is unavailable here is
# unavailable to the keyboard and the palette too — and says why.

tree .
refresh
shot 01-start

# --- Selection ---

assert-selected 0
run select.all
assert-selected 8
run select.none
assert-selected 0
select notes.txt
run select.invert
assert-selected 7
run select.files
assert-selected 5
run select.folders
assert-selected 3
run select.none

# The chords are the list's, and Ctrl+A stays the text box's while somebody types.
assert-key Ctrl+A list select.all
assert-key Ctrl+A text none
assert-key Ctrl+I list select.invert
assert-key Num+ list select.pattern
assert-key Num+ other none
# A dialog, so a run reports it rather than opening one nobody could dismiss.
key Num+
dialog select-pattern 02-select-pattern

# --- View ---

run view.sort-size
run view.sort-reverse
run view.sort-name
shot 03-sorted-by-name
run view.toggle-thumbnails
assert-command view.thumbnails unavailable already
run view.thumbs-larger
shot 04-thumbnails
run view.details
assert-command view.details unavailable already
assert-command view.thumbs-smaller unavailable details

assert-no-row .hidden-notes.txt
key Ctrl+H
assert-row .hidden-notes.txt
key Ctrl+H
assert-no-row .hidden-notes.txt

# --- The other pane ---

assert-command pane.swap unavailable no other pane
assert-command pane.copy-to-other unavailable Nothing is selected
select notes.txt
assert-command pane.copy-to-other unavailable no other pane
deselect

# With one pane, "open this folder in the other pane" makes the other pane.
enter Documents
key Ctrl+Shift+O
assert-panes 2
shot 05-two-panes

# Focus stayed where it was; the new pane shows the same folder. Send it somewhere else.
pane 2
go .
pane 1
assert-path Documents

# Copy and move across, through the same planner a drop uses — so undo works.
select-all
assert-selected 4
key Ctrl+Shift+F5
settle 500
pane 2
refresh
assert-row letter.txt
assert-row draft.md
shot 06-copied-across
pane 1

run pane.swap
shot 07-swapped
run pane.swap
run pane.equalise

# Not during a comparison: its left and right are fixed when it starts, and Sync writes to "the
# right side" — swapping the panes would point that at the other folder.
pane 2
go Pictures
pane 1
compare
assert-command pane.swap unavailable Stop comparing first
assert-command tab.move-to-other-pane unavailable Stop comparing first
compare-end
assert-command pane.swap available

# A tab sent next door takes its folder with it.
newtab .
assert-tabs 2
run tab.move-to-other-pane
assert-tabs 2
pane 1
assert-tabs 1
closepane
assert-panes 1

# --- Go ---

go Documents
run nav.drive-root
assert-command nav.drive-root unavailable already
back
assert-path Documents
assert-command nav.containing-folder unavailable search results or a flat view

# In a flat view the row's real folder is one command away.
up
flat on
assert-flat
select report.md
assert-command nav.containing-folder available
run nav.containing-folder
settle 400
assert-not-flat
assert-row report.md
assert-selected 1

# --- Tabs ---

newtab Documents
newtab Pictures
tab 1
assert-command tab.move-left unavailable first tab
run tab.move-right
run tab.close-right
assert-tabs 2

assert-not-launched
